# Plan: Grid view — see many sessions at one time (D32 proposal)

## Status: proposed, waiting approval — decisions in §3.4 CONFIRMED by the user (D32): interactive cells · move-on-duplicate · uniform cell sizes · picker with no auto-fill
Date: 2026-10-25
Request (user, 2026-10-25): "view many session one time. by choose view with 1x1, 2x1, 1x2, 2x2 or 2x3, 3x2. each sub-window i want can choose session i want to see."

## 1. Goal

A **grid view** of terminals: the user picks a preset layout
(`1x1, 2x1, 1x2, 2x2, 2x3, 3x2` — up to 6 panes) and assigns a session to every
sub-window. Each cell is a **real, interactive terminal** of that session (not a
read-only mirror like the OpenCode worker tabs). Cells are chosen independently,
so the user can watch 2–6 sessions live on one screen.

## 2. What the current code already gives us (verified in source)

| Fact | Where | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| Split panes are renderer-only: pure logic + reducer hook + `TerminalWorkspace` renders panes from `layout.paneIds` | `src/renderer/split/splitLogic.ts`, `useSplitLayout.ts`, `src/renderer/Terminal/TerminalWorkspace.tsx` | The grid needs **no main-process change and no shared-contract change** — same freedom as split. |
| One xterm per session, mounted for the session's whole life, hidden when not visible; live data is ONE subscription dispatched by id | `useTerminalPanes.ts` | 6 cells can coexist; writing to hidden/inactive cells keeps flowing. |
| WebGL renderer with a context-loss fallback | `paneFactory.ts` | 6 WebGL xterm instances is below Chromium's context budget (~16); safe. |
| Panes are created lazily the first time a session becomes visible; `fitPanes`/refit on layout change is already event-driven | `useTerminalPanes.ts`, `TerminalWorkspace.tsx` | Showing a session in a 2nd cell and grid→smaller presets just work. |
| Per-mode storage keys (Ops vs Code keep separate tabs/split/views) | `mode/modeLogic.ts`, `useWorkspaceNav.ts`, `viewPref.ts` | Ops and Code get independent grids, matching D31 practice. |
| `TerminalPane` takes `handleViewportRef`/`visible`/`multi`/`onFocus` as props and renders its header via `SplitPaneHeader` | `TerminalPane.tsx`, `SplitPaneHeader.tsx` | Grid cells can reuse `TerminalPane` with a new header variant. |

Hard limits that must be respected:
- `MAX_PANES = 4` in split — the grid is its own layout type with its own max (6), split stays untouched.
- `useTerminalPanes` keys panes by session id — a session can occupy **at most one cell** (same rule as split dedupes).
- A Closed session has no running pty; cells hold **open sessions only** (reopen first from the sidebar).

## 3. Design

### 3.1 New folder `src/renderer/grid/`

**`gridLogic.ts`** (pure, no React/DOM/IPC — same discipline as `splitLogic.ts`):

```ts
export type GridPreset = '1x1' | '2x1' | '1x2' | '2x2' | '2x3' | '3x2'
export interface GridLayout {
  preset: GridPreset
  cells: readonly (Id | null)[]   // row-major; length = rows * cols
}
export const GRID_MAX_CELLS = 6
```

Pure functions: `presetShape(preset) → {rows, cols}`,
`presetLayout(preset)`, `normalizeGrid(layout, openIds)` (drops dead/duplicate
ids, keeps `null` = empty cell, shrinks nothing), `setCell(layout, index, id|null)`
(clears the id from its previous cell — no duplicates),
`focusCells/indexFor(focusedPane)` helpers,
`parseGrid/serializeGrid` (malformed stored JSON → `null`, same fallback
pattern as `splitLogic.parseLayout`).
Storage key: `sessiondeck.grid.v1` (+ `.code` suffix per mode, like split).

**`useGridLayout.ts`** — reducer + persistence hook, mirroring `useSplitLayout`:
persist on layout change, `sync` with open ids + activeId, actions `setPreset`,
`setCell`, `clearCell`, `focusCell(index)`.

**`GridView.tsx`** — CSS grid (`grid-template-columns/rows` from the preset,
gap = existing split-divider width for the Orca look). Renders `TerminalPane`
per cell (same component → same xterm lifecycle), plus for empty cells a
`GridCellEmpty` with a session picker. All cells share the pane registry
passed down from the workspace (below).

**`GridCellHeader.tsx`** — grid variant of `SplitPaneHeader`: session name
(dropdown listing open sessions: name + status + attention bell — click swaps
the cell's session), restart button, unassign (× clears the cell).
Right-click context menu: same picker + "close session" (match existing pane menu).

### 3.2 Where it lives: a fourth view (`MainView 'grid'`)

Recommended over "grid-as-split-mode": zero interference with split state
(4-pane row split is preserved while the user works in the grid, and comes back
when they switch back), and `viewPref` already persists a per-mode `MainView`.

- `mode/viewPref.ts`: `MainView` gains `'grid'`.
- `useWorkspaceNav.ts`: exposes `grid: GridApi` (`useGridLayout`, keys from
  `modeStorageKeys`), passes grid cells instead of `split.layout.paneIds` as the
  visible ids; `selectSession`/`activateTab` inside grid view focus the session's
  cell (and just record activeId) instead of forcing the terminal view.
- `TerminalWorkspace` and `GridView` share ONE `useTerminalPanes` instance:
  hoist that hook call up into `ModeWorkspace.tsx` (or a small shared wrapper)
  and pass `{panesRef, handleViewportRef, fitPanes, focusPane, createdIds}` down
  to whichever layout is rendered. This keeps "one xterm per session" true even
  when the user flips between split and grid during a session.
- `shell/tab bar`: a view group next to the existing split buttons:
  **Grid ▾** (preset menu: 1x1 · 2x1 · 1x2 · 2x2 · 2x3 · 3x2). Selecting a
  preset switches `view → 'grid'`; "Tabs" / "Split right/down" return to
  terminal; Hub unchanged.
- Focus behaviour (attention, typing target, sleep "on screen" semantics): the
  focused cell's session becomes `activeId` (`window.api.clearAttention` +
  `session:setActive` already follow it). Typing goes to the focused cell only.
- Focus requests (tray/notification/away summary): if the session sits in a
  grid cell, focus that cell and stay in grid; otherwise the existing
  "switch to terminal view" path is used.

### 3.3 Empty cells (fewer open sessions than the preset)

- Never auto-scan or auto-fill: the cell shows "Pick a session" — a searchable
  picker of open sessions (Orca `command` primitive, same feel as the palette),
  filtered by the mode, bellumbled first, keyboard navigable, recent sessions
  first (reuse the palette's `paletteFilter` ranking).
- Changing the preset to a larger one keeps existing assignments and adds empty
  cells; shrinking trims from the end but **keeps a shrinking-safe assignment
  list** only if all truncated cells fit elsewhere — otherwise it keeps the ids
  in a hidden `overflow` so switching back to the bigger preset restores them.
  (Recommendation: keep `overflow` in memory only, not persisted.)

### 3.4 Scoping, decisions to confirm

| # | Question | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| D-a | Grid cells are fully interactive terminals (yes) vs read-only mirrors | Interactive — that is the point vs worker tabs. Yes for all 6 cells. |
| D-b | A session may appear in at most one cell at a time | Yes — one xterm per session is an existing invariant. |
| D-c | Cells hold open sessions only (Closed must be reopened first) | Yes for v1. |
| D-d | Cell sizes are uniform per grid (no draggable dividers) | Yes for v1; presets are the user's chosen shape. Resize can be a later request. |
| D-e | Extra keyboard shortcut (e.g. Ctrl+Shift+G toggles grid) | Skip for v1; the view button + command palette are enough. Palette item "Open grid view" only. |
| D-f | Per-mode grid (Ops and Code remember separate grids) | Yes — matches D31 storage-key practice. |

## 4. Files touched

New: `src/renderer/grid/gridLogic.ts` · `gridLogic.test.ts` ·
`useGridLayout.ts` · `useGridLayout.test.ts` · `GridView.tsx` ·
`GridCellHeader.tsx` · `GridCellEmpty.tsx` · `Terminal/grid-testable.ts` helpers
if hoisting needs them · `scripts/e2e-grid.cjs`.

Changed (small): `mode/viewPref.ts` (add `'grid'`) · `mode/useWorkspaceNav.ts`
(grid API + view switch) · `mode/ModeWorkspace.tsx` (hoist `useTerminalPanes`,
pass registry to both workspaces) · `Terminal/TerminalWorkspace.tsx`
(accept the registry, keep behaviour identical when it owns it) ·
`shell` view buttons (Grid ▾ preset control) · `palette/paletteItems.ts`
